 *     tag-checked and retagged in place.
 *   - source is DMA-owned: no handle exists by construction, so the
 *     slot is named by index and the resulting handle comes back by
 *     value — the shape `pool_acquire_for_encode` already uses, with
 *     `INVALID_HANDLE` as the failure sentinel. The move is a
 *     compare-and-swap of the slot's word from the state it leaves, so a
 *     spurious or replayed signal advances nothing.
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

{% for t in seam %}
{% if t.from_holdable %}
/* `{{ t.from_spec }} -> {{ t.to_spec }}` — {{ t.trigger }}.
 * Spec §synth-5-E line {{ t.spec_line }}. Runtime-owned: call it only
 * once the named hardware event has been observed for this slot.
 * Tag check: handle must be in `SCE_SLOT_{{ t.from_c }}`. Returns
 * `false` on mismatch, leaving every state untouched. */
{{ analyzer["_" ~ t.op_name] }}
